menu "RevLink safety"

config REVLINK_WIFI_SCAN_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "TEST ONLY: scan with the onboard ESP32-C6 radio"
    default n
    help
        Starts the ESP32-P4 to ESP32-C6 hosted Wi-Fi transport over the
        board's 4-bit SDIO link and performs one bounded station scan.

        The test never accepts credentials, joins a network, persists Wi-Fi
        configuration, starts an access point or server, or logs SSIDs/BSSIDs.
        Only the detected AP count, strongest RSSI, and strongest channel are
        reported. It is independent of AccessPort USB and device writes.

        Leave disabled except during the radio coexistence acceptance test.

config REVLINK_WIFI_JOIN_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "TEST ONLY: accept one ephemeral Wi-Fi join from the local console"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_WIFI_SCAN_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on REVLINK_DEV_CONSOLE
    help
        Adds a local-only "wifi-join" development command. The command reads
        an SSID and password without echoing either value, stores them only in
        RAM, attempts one bounded station association and DHCP cycle, and
        performs one fixed DNS lookup after connection.

        Credentials are never written to NVS, microSD, logs, source, or the
        firmware image. No hotspot or server is started. This test is
        independent of AccessPort USB and cannot authorize a device write.

        Leave disabled except during the controlled radio connection
        acceptance test.

config REVLINK_NETWORK_RUNTIME_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "TEST ONLY: run client-first network policy with hotspot fallback"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_WIFI_JOIN_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on REVLINK_DEV_CONSOLE
    help
        Connects the platform-neutral revlink_network coordinator to the
        onboard ESP32-C6 radio adapter. A saved station is preferred;
        failed or unavailable station connectivity falls back to a WPA2
        hotspot named RevLink-<factory MAC suffix>.

        The local console supplies both station and hotspot credentials
        without echo. A station credential is persisted only after successful
        association; the rotating hotspot credential remains RAM-only.
        Credentials are never logged or returned by an API. Network changes
        are rejected while a file transfer is active. This profile starts no
        public internet service and cannot authorize an AccessPort write.

        Leave disabled except during controlled product-network acceptance.

config REVLINK_ONBOARDING_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "TEST ONLY: serve local Wi-Fi onboarding and captive discovery"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_NETWORK_RUNTIME_ACCEPTANCE
    help
        Serves a bounded local onboarding page and JSON API on port 80,
        answers captive DNS only while the private fallback hotspot is ready,
        and advertises a unique revlink-xxxxxx.local mDNS hostname.

        Credential submission is accepted only from hotspot mode while no
        file transfer is active. It requires a non-simple request header,
        applies strict body limits, never logs credentials, and hands them
        directly to the network runtime after the HTTP response. A working
        station credential is saved atomically in NVS and reused after normal
        restart and firmware update. Failed credentials never replace the last
        working record. Hardware-backed encrypted NVS remains a production
        key/eFuse acceptance requirement.
        It does not enable AccessPort writes or public-internet access.

config REVLINK_SD_SPI_TRANSPORT
    bool "Use SPI3 for microSD instead of the SD/MMC controller"
    default y if REVLINK_WIFI_SCAN_ACCEPTANCE
    default n
    help
        Routes the onboard microSD socket through SPI3 using its existing
        wires: CLK GPIO43, MOSI/CMD GPIO44, MISO/D0 GPIO39, and CS/D3 GPIO42.

        This frees the P4 SD/MMC controller for the onboard ESP32-C6 hosted
        Wi-Fi SDIO link. The OLED remains isolated on SPI2. Filesystem and
        cache behavior are unchanged, and automatic formatting remains
        independently locked.

config REVLINK_STATUS_OLED
    bool "Enable the 1.3-inch SH1106 SPI status display"
    default n
    help
        Drives the removable 128x64 SH1106 prototype OLED through the 40-pin
        expansion header. The P4 adapter uses GPIO23 SCLK, GPIO22 MOSI,
        GPIO21 CS, GPIO20 D/C, and GPIO2 RESET. It never owns USB, microSD,
        Wi-Fi SDIO, audio, or strapping pins.

        Display failure is non-fatal and cannot authorize a sync or write.

config REVLINK_STATUS_OLED_ROTATE_180
    bool "Rotate the SH1106 status display 180 degrees"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_STATUS_OLED
    help
        Reverses both the SH1106 segment remap and COM scan direction so the
        complete display is rotated in hardware without transforming the
        framebuffer. Enable this in a board-specific sdkconfig overlay when
        the enclosure mounts the OLED upside down.

config REVLINK_DEV_CONSOLE
    bool "Enable the local UART development control console"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_RUNTIME_SYNC
    help
        Adds a fixed-command UART adapter for status, manual read-only sync,
        cooperative cancel, and saved auto-sync policy. It calls the same
        transport-neutral revlink_control service that the portal's HTTP
        adapter also uses; a BLE adapter would be a third.

        The parser accepts no paths, filenames, upload, delete, format, or
        arbitrary protocol command.

        It is not credential-free. With REVLINK_WIFI_JOIN_ACCEPTANCE also
        enabled — as it is in the shipped Nano profile — the `wifi-join`
        command reads an SSID and a password from this UART. They are read
        with echo suppressed and zeroised after use, but anyone with physical
        access to the programming port can set the Wi-Fi credentials. Treat
        the port as trusted-physical-access only.

config REVLINK_LOCAL_METADATA_BACKFILL_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "MAINTENANCE ONLY: repair development Initial sync timestamps"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_DEV_CONSOLE
    help
        Adds local-UART maintenance commands for zero-only legacy backfill and
        an owner-directed datalog20..58,1,2 filename-wrap resequence in the
        last unambiguous microSD device namespace. Both require explicit Unix
        time inputs and use the existing atomic manifest/history writers.

        It never communicates with or writes to the AccessPort, and it never
        changes cached file bytes, paths, hashes, device timestamps, or notes.
        Leave disabled in normal firmware.

config REVLINK_RUNTIME_SYNC
    bool "Build the bounded runtime datalog-sync coordinator"
    default y
    depends on REVLINK_USB_ROOT_PORT_POWER
    help
        Builds the normal event-driven read-only synchronization path.
        Merely enabling this capability does not start a file session.
        A session must be requested manually or by the saved auto-sync policy.

        Every session retains the accepted four-file, 16 MiB, no-retry bounds.
        This option does not enable uploads, deletes, live data, or any
        AccessPort storage write.

config REVLINK_SYNC_AUTO_ON_ATTACH_DEFAULT
    bool "Default auto-sync policy for unconfigured devices"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_RUNTIME_SYNC
    help
        Used only when the persistent auto-sync setting has never been saved.
        Leave disabled for shipping and development defaults. A user may later
        opt in through the runtime settings API.

config REVLINK_USB_ROOT_PORT_POWER
    bool "Power the high-speed USB Host root port at startup"
    default n
    help
        Enables logical power on ESP32-P4 USB peripheral 0, the high-speed
        OTG 2.0 root port.

        Leave disabled until the USB-A port is empty and the no-load VBUS
        stage has been verified. This setting does not substitute for a
        protected, current-limited external VBUS path.

config REVLINK_USB_INTERFACE_CLAIM_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "Claim and release AccessPort interface 0 without transfers"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_USB_ROOT_PORT_POWER
    help
        After descriptor acceptance succeeds, claim interface 0, allocate its
        endpoint pipes, and immediately release the interface. This gate does
        not submit a bulk transfer or proprietary AccessPort request.

        Leave disabled except during the explicitly authorized interface
        lifecycle acceptance test.

config REVLINK_USB_ROOT_LIST_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "TEST ONLY: perform one bounded read-only root listing"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_USB_ROOT_PORT_POWER
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_INTERFACE_CLAIM_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_IDLE_RELEASE_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_ALLOW_DEVICE_WRITES
    help
        After descriptor acceptance succeeds for a newly attached physical
        device, claim interface 0 and transmit exactly one capture-verified
        empty-path 0x1626 directory-list request on endpoint 0x03. Read at
        most 8192 bytes from endpoint 0x82 with a hard deadline, validate the
        response frame and checksum, parse the complete listing payload, then
        release the interface. A detach followed by a new attach creates a
        fresh bounded acceptance session without rebooting the board.

        There are no retries and no file-content, upload, delete, live-data,
        reset, or disconnect transactions. Leave disabled after this
        separately authorized read-only acceptance test.

config REVLINK_USB_DOWNLOAD_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "TEST ONLY: cache one bounded datalog to microSD"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_USB_ROOT_PORT_POWER
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_INTERFACE_CLAIM_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_ROOT_LIST_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_IDLE_RELEASE_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_ALLOW_DEVICE_WRITES
    depends on !REVLINK_SD_FORMAT_ACCEPTANCE
    help
        For each newly attached physical device, claim interface 0 once, list
        the datalog directory once, select the smallest non-empty .csv or
        .csv.gz file no larger than 8 MiB, and perform one capture-verified
        0x1620/0x1621 read-only download.

        File bytes are streamed through a bounded decoder into a temporary
        microSD file. Protocol framing, declared size, trailer integrity,
        persisted size, fsync, SHA-256, and atomic rename must all succeed
        before the cache file becomes visible. There are no retries and no
        AccessPort upload, delete, live-data, reset, or disconnect commands.

        Leave disabled except during the separately authorized read-only
        download acceptance test.

config REVLINK_USB_INCREMENTAL_SYNC_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "TEST ONLY: incrementally cache bounded datalogs to microSD"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_USB_ROOT_PORT_POWER
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_INTERFACE_CLAIM_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_ROOT_LIST_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_DOWNLOAD_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_IDLE_RELEASE_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_ALLOW_DEVICE_WRITES
    depends on !REVLINK_SD_FORMAT_ACCEPTANCE
    help
        For each newly attached physical device, claim interface 0 once and
        list the datalog directory once. Verify manifest-matching cache entries
        by SHA-256 and skip them. Download at most four missing or changed
        files and at most 16 MiB per attachment session, using the same bounded
        streaming decoder and atomic cache sink proven by the one-file
        acceptance test.

        Each successful file publishes a complete manifest snapshot through
        flush, fsync, and atomic rename. Interrupted temporary files never
        become cache entries, and a later session resumes from the last
        published manifest. Session cleanup releases the selected per-device
        storage namespace so a later attachment cannot inherit stale state.
        There are no retries and no AccessPort upload, delete, live-data,
        reset, or disconnect commands.

        Leave disabled except during a separately authorized read-only
        incremental-sync acceptance test.

config REVLINK_USB_SESSION_CLOSE_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "TEST ONLY: send one capture-verified polite session close"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_USB_ROOT_PORT_POWER
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_INTERFACE_CLAIM_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_ROOT_LIST_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_DOWNLOAD_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_INCREMENTAL_SYNC_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_IDLE_RELEASE_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_ALLOW_DEVICE_WRITES
    help
        For a newly attached AccessPort, claim interface 0 and send exactly
        one capture-verified mini subtype 0x05 session-close request. Wait
        briefly for subtype 0x35, then release the interface. The AccessPort
        normally performs a software re-enumeration roughly 0.6 seconds later.

        This operation does not list, download, upload, delete, reset storage,
        or modify any AccessPort file. Leave disabled except during an
        explicitly authorized session-lifecycle acceptance test.

config REVLINK_USB_IDLE_RELEASE_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "TEST ONLY: release the logical USB root port after enumeration"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_USB_ROOT_PORT_POWER
    help
        After descriptor-only AccessPort acceptance, wait five seconds and
        stop the ESP-IDF logical root port. This submits no proprietary or
        bulk transaction. It exists only to determine whether removing the
        active data link is sufficient for the AccessPort to return to
        Gauges while it remains powered from the vehicle.

        This cannot control physical USB-A VBUS on the Waveshare development
        board. Leave disabled in normal firmware.

config REVLINK_USB_PC_MODE_EXIT_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "TEST ONLY: sync, politely close, and release the USB root port"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_RUNTIME_SYNC
    depends on REVLINK_USB_ROOT_PORT_POWER
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_INTERFACE_CLAIM_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_ROOT_LIST_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_DOWNLOAD_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_INCREMENTAL_SYNC_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_SESSION_CLOSE_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_IDLE_RELEASE_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_ALLOW_DEVICE_WRITES
    help
        Force one auto-sync for a newly attached AccessPort. After the normal
        bounded read-only sync path sends the capture-verified mini subtype
        0x05 close, releases interface 0, and publishes its terminal event,
        stop the logical USB root port.

        This exists only to verify that a complete host lifecycle returns the
        still-powered AccessPort to Gauges without a physical unplug. It does
        not enable uploads, deletes, formatting, live-data commands, or any
        AccessPort storage write.

config REVLINK_USB_SESSION_CYCLE_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "TEST ONLY: repeat acknowledged sync/eject lifecycle"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_RUNTIME_SYNC
    depends on REVLINK_USB_ROOT_PORT_POWER
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_PC_MODE_EXIT_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_INTERFACE_CLAIM_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_ROOT_LIST_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_DOWNLOAD_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_INCREMENTAL_SYNC_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_SESSION_CLOSE_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_IDLE_RELEASE_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_ALLOW_DEVICE_WRITES
    help
        Force one initial read-only auto-sync, then repeat the normal bounded
        sync only after each acknowledged 0x05/0x35 close has produced a
        software detach, fresh high-speed enumeration, and accepted
        descriptor scan. Stop after the configured count or on the first
        failed/cancelled session.

        This validates that normal sessions return the AccessPort to Gauges
        without a cable unplug, manual D+/D- switch, root-port shutdown,
        upload, delete, format, live-data request, or storage write.

config REVLINK_USB_SESSION_CYCLE_ACCEPTANCE_COUNT
    int "Acknowledged lifecycle repetitions"
    range 2 20
    default 5
    depends on REVLINK_USB_SESSION_CYCLE_ACCEPTANCE

config REVLINK_USB_CLOSE_RECOVERY_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "TEST ONLY: inject one unclean close and recover once"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_RUNTIME_SYNC
    depends on REVLINK_USB_ROOT_PORT_POWER
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_SESSION_CYCLE_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_PC_MODE_EXIT_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_INTERFACE_CLAIM_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_ROOT_LIST_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_DOWNLOAD_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_INCREMENTAL_SYNC_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_SESSION_CLOSE_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_USB_IDLE_RELEASE_ACCEPTANCE
    depends on !REVLINK_ALLOW_DEVICE_WRITES
    help
        Force one initial read-only sync, deliberately omit its polite close,
        and verify that the application queues exactly one bounded initialized
        session-close recovery. The recovery must finish with an acknowledged
        0x05/0x35 close and software re-enumeration.

        This fault-injection mode does not upload, delete, format, issue
        live-data requests, reset the USB bus, toggle D+/D-, or modify any
        AccessPort file. Leave disabled in normal firmware.

config REVLINK_ALLOW_DEVICE_WRITES
    bool "Permit AccessPort write transactions"
    default y
    depends on REVLINK_RUNTIME_SYNC
    depends on REVLINK_USB_ROOT_PORT_POWER
    help
        Compiles the guarded microSD-backed map-upload transport. New and
        factory-reset Sidecars start with owner consent disabled. Once changed
        in Settings, that preference persists until the owner changes it.
        Destinations are allowlisted, the attached AccessPort identity is
        pinned, and an upload is successful only after a fresh download
        matches the source SHA-256.

        This does not enable deletion. The same target-validated, staged,
        identity-pinned, and read-back-verified service also carries the exact
        images/startup_screen.fb workflow.

config REVLINK_ALLOW_DEVICE_DELETES
    bool "Permit AccessPort file deletion"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_ALLOW_DEVICE_WRITES
    help
        Compiles the guarded delete path for files directly inside maps/ and
        datalog/. Nothing else is deletable: not images/, not the directories
        themselves, not anything nested.

        Deletion is irreversible. The AccessPort offers no undo and RevLink
        keeps no copy of what it removes beyond whatever the Sidecar had
        already synchronised. Every delete pins the target device by part
        number and serial, requires the file to be present first, and re-lists
        the directory afterwards to confirm the entry is gone.

        Owner consent for deletion is separate from write consent and is not
        implied by it: agreeing to transfer maps onto a device is not agreeing
        to let this remove files from it.

        Accepted on hardware and compiled into the Nano product profile. The
        runtime consent is separate, starts locked, and is what actually
        permits a delete.

config REVLINK_MAP_AUTO_APPLY_DEFAULT
    bool "Default staged-map auto-apply preference to enabled"
    default n
    depends on REVLINK_ALLOW_DEVICE_WRITES
    help
        A map can be uploaded to the Sidecar while no AccessPort is attached.
        It is stored on microSD together with its SHA-256 and the identity of
        the AccessPort it was staged for, and it survives a power cycle.

        When auto-apply is enabled, that staged map is written during the next
        attach, but only after a clean and complete read-only sync, and only
        if the attached AccessPort's part number and serial both match the
        recorded target. A map staged for one car is never written to another.

        This is only the factory default for the owner preference. It has no
        effect unless write consent is also enabled in Settings, and one
        automatic attempt is made per attach: a failed write is never retried
        automatically.

        Leave disabled unless the controlled round-trip in
        docs/MAP_WRITE_ACCEPTANCE.md has been completed on real hardware.

config REVLINK_WRITE_ACCEPTANCE_PART_NUMBER
    string "Write-acceptance AccessPort part-number pin"
    default ""
    depends on REVLINK_ALLOW_DEVICE_WRITES
    help
        Optional build-time identity pin for a controlled write-acceptance
        image. When set, every upload is refused unless the authoritative
        device identity exactly matches this part number. The donor acceptance
        build pins AP3-VLK-002. This does not replace serial pinning, which is
        captured separately for each runtime operation.

config REVLINK_SD_FORMAT_ACCEPTANCE
    bool "DESTRUCTIVE: format and provision the microSD card once"
    default n
    help
        Erases and formats the onboard microSD card as FAT, creates the RevLink
        directory layout, and runs a write, flush, atomic rename, unmount,
        remount, and SHA-256 verification test.

        Enable only for an explicitly authorized acceptance flash. Disable and
        reflash immediately after the test so a later mount failure can never
        trigger an automatic format.

endmenu
